  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing the Recommendations from the High Level Panel on Social Protection (FALSOC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Context for the assignment: In 2025 the UK and Somalia co-chaired a High-Level Panel on Social Protection in Fragile and Conflict Affected Settings, which launched its recommendations on 4 November in Doha. This ambitious initiative seeks to catalyse global action and support for social protection in those contexts where needs are highest. The next stage in the Panel process is taking forward the recommendations and call to action through development and implementation of a communications campaign and strategic influencing plan for 2026. 

To date, the High-Level Panel has benefitted from technical assistance and communications support provided by DAI through the STAAR facility under the BASIC programme, which closes in December 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
